==Problem==

Quadrilateral <imath>ABCD</imath> with side lengths <imath>AB=7, BC=24, CD=20, DA=15</imath> is inscribed in a circle. The area interior to the circle but exterior to the quadrilateral can be written in the form <imath>\frac{a\pi-b}{c},</imath> where <imath>a,b,</imath> and <imath>c</imath> are positive integers such that <imath>a</imath> and <imath>c</imath> have no common prime factor. What is <imath>a+b+c?</imath>

<imath>\textbf{(A) } 260 \qquad \textbf{(B) } 855 \qquad \textbf{(C) } 1235 \qquad \textbf{(D) } 1565 \qquad \textbf{(E) } 1997</imath>

